@startuml
title Embers frontend — test tiers and what each one can observe
skinparam backgroundColor #FFF8F2
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #5B3A29
skinparam defaultFontColor #2B1D17
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDFB
  BorderColor #A85C32
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF5
  BorderColor #A85C32
}

rectangle "Tier 1 — unit and integration (jest)" as t1 #FFE1A8 {
  component "example-based\napps/embers, packages/*" as unit #FFFDFB
  component "property-based\nfast-check" as props #FFFDFB
  component "query-layer integration\nreal SDK, injected transport" as integ #FFFDFB
}

rectangle "Tier 2 — browser (Playwright)" as t2 #B9DCF7 {
  component "mock backend\nin-process, per test" as mock #FFFDFB
  component "journeys\nauth, dashboard, deletion" as journeys #FFFDFB
  component "media capture\nscreenshots for docs" as media #FFFDFB
}

rectangle "Tier 3 — live stack (opt-in)" as t3 #C8E6C9 {
  component "API conformance\n55 operations" as conf #FFFDFB
  component "smoke journeys\nreal chain" as smoke #FFFDFB
}

note right of t1
  Observes: logic, protocol,
  state transitions, invariants.
  BLIND TO: geometry and colour.
  jsdom performs no layout and
  resolves no custom properties,
  so every box measures zero and
  every computed colour is empty.
end note

note right of t2
  Observes: everything tier 1 does,
  plus what the user actually sees.
  Found the zero-width delete icon
  and the invisible Cancel label —
  neither reachable from jsdom.
end note

note right of t3
  Observes: the real contract.
  Needs a running node, so it is
  never what CI runs.
end note

t1 -[#5B3A29]-> t2 : fast feedback first
t2 -[#5B3A29]-> t3 : contract confirmed last

@enduml
